VERDICT -- head2head
====================
THE NEW BUILD IS NOT AN IMPROVEMENT ON THE BINARIES THAT ACTUALLY SHIP.

      old med      new med     delta   paired per draw     new wins
  P1     518,660     571,668   +10.2%   +10.2 +12.5 -5.6      1/3
  P3   4,609,668   4,496,780   - 2.4%   - 1.3 - 4.6 -3.1      3/3
  six paired cells: ratio-mean +1.37%, geo-mean +1.11%, new 4/6 by count and behind by size

WHY THIS CONTRADICTS EVERYTHING MEASURED TODAY.  harness/run1.py imports from the recon directory,
whose cpython-312 extensions are dated 2026-08-07.  build_submission.sh compiles the five engines
from source into the package.  The dirgate zip and today's zip carry BYTE-IDENTICAL .so files
despite being built days apart, which proves the build is reproducible and therefore that the
repo's differing .so are a genuinely different source state, not a rebuild artefact.

    ogc_fast   repo a584fd58...  zip c1398aba...
    ogc_geom   repo ea221ad6...  zip 85d27113...
    ogc_state  repo 0e874d9e...  zip 01db30d1...
    cranepack  repo 99fb5314...  zip 6bea522b...
    st3dtcs    repo 5cc39d58...  zip 9aa807a1...

So rfship, rf4, gaterf, w3rf, rounds05 and wdef all ran a four-day-old engine.  Each experiment was
internally fair -- both arms imported the same stale .so -- but nothing verified that the effects
transfer to the engine in the submission, and on P1 they do not.

THE SAME CONFIGURATION, TWO ENGINES:
    P1, RESFRAC 0.50, nw=3   stale engine (wdef arm A)   688,254 / 708,344 / 754,716
                             shipped engine (this test)  508,193 / 518,660 / 605,585

The shipped engine is roughly 30% better on P1 at the OLD setting, which is most of what the
reserve change appeared to buy.  wdef's -17.36% was measuring headroom that the shipped engine had
already closed.

WHAT IS STILL STANDING.  The CPU cap is untouched by this: it follows from the organisers' notice
that 400% is enforced by throttling with every core visible, and from os.cpu_count() being the
wrong number in that setting.  It is not supported by any of the stale-engine measurements and
never was.

WHAT TO DO.  Rebuild the recon extensions from source so the harness imports the shipped engine,
then re-run the reserve A/B on the six firing instances.  Until that is done the submitted
OGC2026_dirgate.zip stands and OGC2026_capfix.zip must not be submitted.
